From: Numerio <b.vitruvio@gmail.com>
Subject: link against libm explicitly
Forwarded: not-needed
Description:
 On the legacy platform the math functions (round() et al.) resolved
 through libroot, which pulled in libm. Debian linker does not resolve
 symbols transitively, so the link fails on obj/AirBrushTool.o without
 -lm on the command line.
Author: Numerio <b.vitruvio@gmail.com>

--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -100,7 +100,7 @@
 #		naming scheme you need to specify the path to the library
 #		and it's name
 #		library: my_lib.a entry: my_lib.a or path/my_lib.a
-LIBS= be tracker translation localestub z $(STDCPPLIBS)
+LIBS= be tracker translation localestub z m $(STDCPPLIBS)
 
 #	specify additional paths to directories following the standard
 #	libXXX.so or libXXX.a naming scheme.  You can specify full paths
